==Post-match==
===Trophy presentation and celebrations===
[[File:2010 - UEFA Champions League Trophy.jpg|thumb|329x329px|The UEFA Champions League trophy in [[FC Barcelona Museum]].]]
In a gesture by his teammates, [[Eric Abidal]], who had undergone surgery only two months earlier to remove a tumour in his liver, was given the honour of wearing the captain's armband during the trophy presentation ceremony. He was the first player to lift the trophy. Speaking afterwards, Abidal, who was in tears, appreciated the gesture, and spoke of how "special" his club was.<ref>{{cite news |title=Touching gesture follows Barca's victory |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/soccer/news?slug=ro-rogers_abidal_barcelona_champions_league_cancer_052811 |work=[[Yahoo! Sports]] |last=Rogers |first=Martin |date=28 May 2011 |access-date=29 May 2011}}</ref>

Barcelona coach [[Pep Guardiola]] singled out Messi after the game, stating the Argentine was "the best player [he'd] ever seen" and that Messi "made the difference" in the game.<ref name="guardiola">{{cite news |title=Guardiola delighted with performance |url=http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924245/pep-guardiola-delighted-with-barca-performance?cc=5901 |publisher=[[ESPNsoccernet]] |date=28 May 2011 |access-date=29 May 2011 |archive-date=26 October 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121026105505/http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924245/pep-guardiola-delighted-with-barca-performance?cc=5901 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Meanwhile, Manchester United manager [[Alex Ferguson|Sir Alex Ferguson]] acknowledged that the Barcelona side was the best team he had ever faced.<ref name="best">{{cite news |title=Fergie: Barca the best I've faced |url=http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924246/sir-alex-ferguson%3A-barcelona-the-best-team-i%27ve-faced?cc=5901 |publisher=[[ESPNsoccernet]] |date=28 May 2011 |access-date=29 May 2011 |archive-date=31 May 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110531062541/http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924246/sir-alex-ferguson%3A-barcelona-the-best-team-i%27ve-faced?cc=5901 |url-status=dead }}</ref> His sentiments were echoed by United captain [[Nemanja Vidić]] and defender [[Rio Ferdinand]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Vidic: Barca were deserving winners |url=http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924224/nemanja-vidic:-barcelona-were-deserving-winners?cc=5901 |publisher=[[ESPNsoccernet]] |date=28 May 2011 |access-date=29 May 2011 |archive-date=26 October 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121026105538/http://soccernet.espn.go.com/news/story/_/id/924224/nemanja-vidic:-barcelona-were-deserving-winners?cc=5901 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

[[Gerard Piqué]] cut the mesh from the net in front of the Barcelona fans where Barcelona had scored the two winning goals, and took it back to the club museum at the [[Camp Nou]]. The Barcelona players, coaches, and their families then formed a circle at centre field and danced. The sprinklers at Wembley came on at this time and the players and coaches celebrated under them.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Branch |first=John |date=2011-05-29 |title=Prized Possession for Barcelona: Champions League Title |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/sports/soccer/in-dominant-display-barcelona-wins-champions-league.html |url-access=subscription |access-date=2025-01-06 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

The match was the last for Manchester United goalkeeper [[Edwin van der Sar]], who had announced his retirement from football to follow the 2011 season.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Staff |date=2010-12-23 |title=Manchester United's Edwin van der Sar to retire after this season |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/dec/23/edwin-van-der-sar-retire-season |access-date=2025-01-06 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

==Broadcasting==
The match was shown on [[ITV (TV network)|ITV]] and [[Sky Sports]] in the United Kingdom. Sky Sports partnered with UK-based outside broadcast facilities providers [[NEP Visions]] and Telegenic to produce host coverage of the match.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Champions League Final at Wembley {{!}} LIVE-PRODUCTION.TV |url=https://www.live-production.tv/news/4k-8k-arising/champions-league-final-wembley.html |access-date=2025-01-06 |website=www.live-production.tv}}</ref> In the United States, [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] aired the final for the second consecutive year.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Staff |first=Channel Guide |date=2011-05-17 |title=FOX Sports provides exclusive U.S. coverage of Champions League Final |url=https://www.channelguidemag.com/tv-news/2011/05/17/27928/ |access-date=2025-01-06 |website=Channel Guide Magazine |language=en-US}}</ref> In [[South America]], [[Rede Globo]] and [[Rede Bandeirantes]] broadcast the match for [[Brazil]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2011-05-27 |title=Uefa and Europa League broadcast deals for Brazil |url=https://www.sportspro.com/news/uefa_and_europa_league_broadcast_deals_for_brazil/ |access-date=2025-01-06 |website=SportsPro |language=en-GB}}</ref> [[Sky Deutschland]] (Pay TV) and [[Sat. 1]] were broadcasting the match for [[Germany]], public broadcaster [[SF 2]] showed the final in [[Switzerland]], as well as, the public broadcaster [[ORF 1]] in [[Austria]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://news.tv-sport.de/index.php/live-fc-barcelona-manchester-united-uefa-champions-league-das-finale-in-london-vorbericht-und-liveticker/ |title=Broadcasters from German spoken countries |trans-title=Sky Deutschland, Sat.1, SF 2 and ORF 1 are broadcasting UEFA's Champions League Final 2011 |date=21 May 2011 |language=de |publisher=TV-Sport.de |access-date=23 April 2012 |archive-date=25 August 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110825053145/http://news.tv-sport.de/index.php/live-fc-barcelona-manchester-united-uefa-champions-league-das-finale-in-london-vorbericht-und-liveticker/ |url-status=dead }}</ref>

The match was broadcast live in 3D in the Trädgår'n club hall in [[Gothenburg]], Sweden on the ''[[Guinness World Records|Guinness Book of World Records]]''' largest television.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.ekta-led.com/news/itm/527/ | title=EKTA's Ukrainian produced 3D Led TV makes the Guinness World Record Book | publisher=ekta-led.com | access-date=21 July 2011| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111018191329/http://www.ekta-led.com/news/itm/527/ | archive-date=18 October 2011 | url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.viasat.se/content/press-och-nyhetsrum#/pressrelease/view/viasat-saetter-nytt-guinness-vaerldsrekord-i-3d-tv-657702 |title=Viasat sätter nytt Guinness världsrekord i 3D-TV |trans-title=Viasat sets a new Guinness world record for 3-D TV |date=1 July 2011 |language=sv |publisher=viasat.se |access-date=21 July 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110801005209/http://www.viasat.se/content/press-och-nyhetsrum#/pressrelease/view/viasat-saetter-nytt-guinness-vaerldsrekord-i-3d-tv-657702 |archive-date=1 August 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

